<h2>Context</h2>

<p>Reve Stitching is a knitted-garment manufacturer in Faisalabad serving UK fashion retailers and other international buyers. The first requirement was a credible public presence. The operational problems behind that request were larger: enquiries arrived through disconnected channels, quotes were assembled manually, and buyer activity did not feed into the systems used inside the factory.</p>

<p>I built and maintain the platform end to end while working close to the teams that use it. That access changed the product from a marketing site into a digital operations layer.</p>

<CaseStudyMedia image={homeDesktop} alt="Reve Stitching public homepage with garment manufacturing positioning and quote call to action" caption="01 / The production homepage used to establish credibility with international buyers." />

<h2>The system</h2>

<p><strong>Public experience.</strong> The website presents capabilities, product ranges and manufacturing context through a fast catalogue designed for B2B buyers.</p>

<p><strong>Structured intake.</strong> Quote and sample requests use guided forms with server-side validation, honeypot protection and Cloudflare Turnstile. Submissions become typed operational records rather than loose messages.</p>

<CaseStudyMedia image={quoteIntake} alt="Reve quote request landing page with a guided multi-step intake flow" caption="02 / Quote intake begins with clear expectations and a guided request path." />

<CaseStudyMedia image={quoteWizard} alt="Reve quote wizard product-selection step with specifications and quantity guidance" caption="03 / Structured product selection inside the quote wizard." />

<p><strong>Admin operations.</strong> An authenticated admin area covers quotes, samples, contact enquiries, live chat and follow-up work. The current source contains 13 admin pages and 38 API routes.</p>

<p><strong>Client portal.</strong> Registered clients can access orders, quotes, documents and messages through a separate portal with per-client data boundaries. The current source contains 13 portal pages.</p>

<p><strong>Transactional email and follow-up.</strong> Resend templates cover confirmations, status updates and internal reminders so an enquiry does not disappear after submission.</p>

<p><strong>AI-assisted review.</strong> Incoming quote information can be summarized and reference files can be analyzed for an operator. These are drafts for a person to review, not automatic commercial decisions.</p>

